    <!-- Banners on the System page -->
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.ReadOnlyTitle">Readings only on this laptop</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.ReadOnlyBody">The firmware interface is there, but it did not answer the way the machine this was built against does, so nothing that writes to it is offered:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.UnsupportedTitle">This laptop isn't supported</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.UnsupportedBody">Nextcalibur was built for a specific firmware interface and this machine does not have it. Nothing has been changed, and nothing here will do anything.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.NoAccessTitle">The firmware interface could not be reached</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.NoAccessBody">This laptop has the interface Nextcalibur reads, but Windows did not let this process use it. Reopen Nextcalibur as administrator.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.NoSensorsBody">Nextcalibur can't find the sensors and lighting on this machine, so those pages won't work. Power settings still do.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.NoDriverTitle">The NVIDIA driver is not installed</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.NoDriverBody">The graphics card is there but its driver is not, so the Display page and the card's readings are unavailable until it is back. The laptop maker's driver page is under Settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.VendorOpenTitle">Casper's Control Center is open</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.VendorOpenBody">Both apps are talking to the same hardware, so readings may stall and lighting changes may not stick. Close it and this message will clear itself.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.ProfileCopyTitle">Asked for administrator rights at every start</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Banner.ProfileCopyBody">This copy runs from a folder your account can change, so it cannot be started as administrator without a prompt - that would let anything running as you run as administrator. Install it with the installer from the release page and it goes under Program Files, where the prompt is asked once.</sys:String>

    <!-- Unsupported machine, the vendor's software -->
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Unsupported.Title">Nextcalibur - not supported here</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Unsupported.Body" xml:space="preserve">This laptop does not have the firmware interface Nextcalibur was built for.&#10;&#10;Nothing has been changed on your machine, and to keep it that way, nothing in this window will respond. There is no reason to keep it installed.&#10;&#10;Open Windows' list of installed apps so you can remove it?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Vendor.Title">Nextcalibur - two applications, one interface</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Vendor.Body" xml:space="preserve">{0} is installed on this machine.&#10;&#10;Both it and Nextcalibur talk to the same interface in your laptop's firmware, and it can only handle one request at a time. With both installed, readings stall and lighting changes sometimes fail to apply - in either application.&#10;&#10;Removing it is recommended. Nextcalibur will not do that for you, and it works either way.&#10;&#10;Open Windows' list of installed apps now?&#10;&#10;Choosing No keeps it, and this message will not come back.</sys:String>

